    "DT (days)": {
     "choice": "measured",
     "probs": {
      "measured": 0.949,
      "literature": 0.051
     },
     "said": [
      "Four days after being laid, the eggs were inspected to determine the number of hatched larvae, embryonated eggs (fertile eggs with unsuccessful hatching), and infertile eggs.",
      "Demographic Parameters To calculate the intrinsic rate of increase $( r _ { m } ) ,$ the Euler–Lotka equation was iteratively solved, according to the following equation [27]: $$ 1 = \\sum_ {x = 0} ^ {\\infty} e ^ {- r _ {m} (x + 1)} l _ {x} m _ {x} $$ where x is time (days), $l _ { x }$ is age-specific survival, and $m _ { x }$ is age-specific female offspring (hatched larvae)."
     ],
     "value": "measured"
    },
    "τ (days)": {
     "choice": "measured",
     "probs": {
      "measured": 0.92,
      "literature": 0.08
     },
     "said": [
      "Four days after being laid, the eggs were inspected to determine the number of hatched larvae, embryonated eggs (fertile eggs with unsuccessful hatching), and infertile eggs.",
      "Demographic Parameters To calculate the intrinsic rate of increase $( r _ { m } ) ,$ the Euler–Lotka equation was iteratively solved, according to the following equation [27]: $$ 1 = \\sum_ {x = 0} ^ {\\infty} e ^ {- r _ {m} (x + 1)} l _ {x} m _ {x} $$ where x is time (days), $l _ { x }$ is age-specific survival, and $m _ { x }$ is age-specific female offspring (hatched larvae)."
     ],
     "value": "measured"
    },
    "R_0 (female offspring/female)": {
     "choice": "measured",
     "probs": {
      "measured": 0.985,
      "literature": 0.015
     },
     "said": [
      "Demographic Parameters To calculate the intrinsic rate of increase $( r _ { m } ) ,$ the Euler–Lotka equation was iteratively solved, according to the following equation [27]: $$ 1 = \\sum_ {x = 0} ^ {\\infty} e ^ {- r _ {m} (x + 1)} l _ {x} m _ {x} $$ where x is time (days), $l _ { x }$ is age-specific survival, and $m _ { x }$ is age-specific female offspring (hatched larvae).",
      "The following mathematical formulas were used to calculate the net reproductive rate $( R _ { 0 } ,$ defined as female offspring per female), mean generation time (τ), finite rate of increase (λ), and doubling time (DT): $$ R _ {0} = \\sum l _ {x} m _ {x} $$ $$ \\tau = \\frac {l n R _ {0}}{r _ {m}} $$ Insects 2024, 15, 486 4 of 10 $$ \\lambda = e ^ {r _ {m}} $$ $$ D T = \\frac {\\ln 2}{r _ {m}} $$ Considering that population growth parameters are calculated with the data of several females, it is not possible to statistically compare them directly, because only one value is obtained."
     ],
     "value": "measured"
    }
   }
